sition divided among Democrat Alani Bankhead, independent Seth Bodnar, and a Libertarian. Expert raters unanimously call the race Safe or Solid R, markets price a Democratic win near zero, and Alme holds a decisive money advantage in a state that leans Republican by ten points.", "watch": "A consolidation of the anti-Alme vote behind one challenger, or a major outside-spending surge for Bodnar or Bankhead, could narrow the margin, though a Democratic win remains highly unlikely.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Steve Daines (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Montana's open Senate seat, vacated by retiring Republican Steve Daines, is expected to remain in Republican hands. Kurt Alme has out-raised Democrat Alani Bankhead by a wide margin and benefits from substantial outside spending, while independent Seth Bodnar has drawn some endorsements and funding but polls a distant second. A Libertarian candidate further fragments the opposition.\n\nPolling from June through September consistently shows Alme ahead by roughly 15 to 25 points, with the Democratic nominee stuck in the teens or low twenties. All ten expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give the Democratic side about a one percent chance. The state's ten-point Republican lean and the divided field make an upset improbable.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0053, "margin": -15.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0028, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.004, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0021, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0024, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0027, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0026, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0029, "margin": -19.0}]}